Formgen: Forms can now send the user back to an external application after submitting. If the form is opened with the URL parameter "returnUrl", the load response contains "formSettings" with "returnUrlEnabled": true and the origin of the URL (http or https only) is one of "returnUrlOrigins" (protocol, host and optional port, e.g. "https://app.example.com"), the user is redirected to this URL after submitting instead of seeing the success screen, and also when cancelling the form. The returnUrl takes precedence over the successUrl and the cancel URL. This only applies to the web version.
